# Design documentation (KDD)

The design document for this app is held in **`docs/kdd/`**.

When creating, updating, or citing app design / KDD material, use that folder — not other trees under `docs/` or app-local `docs/` folders — unless the user explicitly points elsewhere.

## Glossary (required)

Every KDD must open with a **Glossary** section (immediately after the title/lede) that defines local terminology used in the doc — code constants (e.g. `WINDOW_RADIUS`), domain shorthand, and project-specific names.

- Only include terms that help **quick readability** of that doc.
- Skip obvious English and terms defined only by a one-off code citation the reader does not need to carry.
- Prefer a compact term/meaning table.

## Project terminology canon

**[`docs/kdd/002-terminology-map.md`](docs/kdd/002-terminology-map.md) (KDD-002)** is the project-wide terminology source of truth (Station; adjacent/neighbouring; Through =2 / Terminal =1 / Junction ≥3; Segment = Route; JunctionSegment / Line; Journey; live-track context vs topology Route; spine; window; etc.). Prefer those definitions in new prose and code; migrate older identifiers over time. Diagrams in KDD-002 are normative for the build-up terms.
